Object.assign(window.TEM8_DICTIONARY, {"gestures":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒestʃə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a movement that you make with your hands, your head or your face to show a particular meaning","cn":"手势；姿势；示意动作"},{"en":"something that you do or say to show a particular feeling or intention （","cn":"表明感情或意图的）姿态，表示"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gesture__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gesture__us_1.mp3"}},"getting":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/getting__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/getting__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈɡetɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"before a situation changes and it is no longer possible to do sth","cn":"趁形势还未变化时；趁情况还有利时"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Getting is the present participle of get ."},{"pos":"PREP-PHRASE 短语介词","cn":"同nearly","en":"Getting on for means the same as nearly .","ex":{"en":"I've been trying to give up smoking for getting on for two years now","cn":"到现在，我设法戒烟已快两年了。"}}]}},"geographical":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geographical__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geographical__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"地理（学）的","en":"Geographical or geographic means concerned with or relating to geography.","ex":{"en":"Its geographical location stimulated overseas mercantile enterprise.","cn":"它的地理位置引起了海外商家的兴趣。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The importance of the town is due to its geographical location.","cn":"这座城镇的重要性在于它的地理位置。"},{"en":"The survey covers a wide geographical area.","cn":"此项调查覆盖的地理区域非常广阔。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒiːəˈɡræfɪkl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"connected with the way in which the physical features of a place are arranged","cn":"与一个地方的物理特征的排列方式有关的","ex":{"en":"The importance of the town is due to its geographical location.","cn":"这个镇的重要性在于其地理位置。"}},{"en":"connected with the scientific study of the earth's surface, physical features, divisions, products, population, etc.","cn":"与地球表面、物理特征、分区、产品、人口等的科学研究有关。","ex":{"en":"Researchers and surveyors exchanged geographical knowledge.","cn":"研究人员和测量员交流地理知识。"}},{"en":"connected with the way in which a particular aspect of life or society is influenced by geography or varies according to geography","cn":"与生活或社会的某一特定方面受地理影响或随地理变化的方式有关的","ex":{"en":"the geographical distribution of wealth","cn":"财富的地理分布"}}]}},"generate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/generate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/generate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to produce energy, especially electricity","cn":"产生（能量）；发（电）","ex":{"en":"The wind turbines are used to generate electricity.","cn":"风力涡轮机被用来发电。"}},{"en":"to produce or create something","cn":"产生；引起","ex":{"en":"to generate revenue/income/profit","cn":"产生收益／收入／利润"}},{"en":"to produce a set or sequence of data by taking an initial set of data and applying a mathematical or logical process to it","cn":"生成：通过对初始数据集进行数学或逻辑处理，生成一组数据或一系列数据。","lab":"computing","ex":{"en":"We generated 10 data sets, which we used to run each of the models.","cn":"我们生成了 10 个数据集，用于运行每个模型。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"造成；引起；导致","en":"To generate something means to cause it to begin and develop.","ex":{"en":"The Employment Minister said the reforms would generate new jobs.","cn":"劳工大臣表示，改革将带来新的就业机会。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"产生（能量）；发（电）","en":"To generate a form of energy or power means to produce it.","ex":{"en":"The company, New England Electric, burns coal to generate power.","cn":"新英格兰电力公司用煤发电。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The proposal has generated a lot of interest.","cn":"这项建议引起众多的关注。"},{"en":"We need someone to generate new ideas.","cn":"我们需要有人出新主意。"}]},"geometry":{"oxford":{"phon":"dʒiˈɒmətri","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the branch of mathematics that deals with the measurements and relationships of lines, angles, surfaces and solids","cn":"几何（学）","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Pre-Christian sacred geometry was incorporated into church architecture.","cn":"西历纪元开始以前的神圣几何被运用于教堂建筑中。"}},{"en":"the measurements and relationships of lines, angles, etc. in a particular object or shape","cn":"几何形状；几何图形；几何结构","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"the geometry of a spider’s web","cn":"蜘蛛网的几何形状"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"几何（学）","en":"Geometry is the branch of mathematics concerned with the properties and relationships of lines, angles, curves, and shapes.","ex":{"en":"...the very ordered way in which mathematics and geometry describe nature.","cn":"数学和几何学极有条理的描述自然的方式"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"形状；外形；几何图形；几何结构","en":"The geometry of an object is its shape or the relationship of its parts to each other.","ex":{"en":"They have tinkered with the geometry of the car's nose.","cn":"他们对车头的外观进行了改进。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geometry__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geometry__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"the geometry of a spider's web","cn":"蜘蛛网的几何形状"}]},"generally":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/generally__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/generally__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenrəli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"by or to most people","cn":"普遍地；广泛地","ex":{"en":"The initiative was generally considered a success.","cn":"这项倡议被普遍认为是成功的。"}},{"en":"in most cases","cn":"一般地；通常；大体上","ex":{"en":"I generally get up at six.","cn":"我一般六点钟起床。"}},{"en":"without discussing the details of something","cn":"笼统地；概括地；大概","ex":{"en":"Let's talk just about investment generally.","cn":"咱们只大概谈谈投资吧。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"笼统地；概括地","en":"You use generally to give a summary of a situation, activity, or idea without referring to the particular details of it.","ex":{"en":"University teachers generally have admitted a lack of enthusiasm about their subjects","cn":"高校教师大体上承认对其所教专业缺乏热情。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"通常地；一般地；普遍地","en":"You use generally to say that something happens or is used on most occasions but not on every occasion.","ex":{"en":"As women we generally say and feel too much about these things","cn":"作为女性，我们通常在这些事情上谈得过多，过于敏锐。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The new drug will be generally available from January.","cn":"这种新药从一月份开始将可广泛使用。"},{"en":"He was a generally unpopular choice for captain.","cn":"人们普遍不欢迎他成为队长的人选。"}]},"gear":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gear__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gear__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ɡɪə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"equipment in a vehicle that changes the relation between engine speed (or pedal speed on a bicycle) and the speed of the wheels moving forwards or backwards","cn":"排挡；齿轮；传动装置","g":"[countable, usually plural]","sc":"in vehicle","ex":{"en":"Careless use of the clutch may damage the gears.","cn":"离合器使用不慎可能会损坏传动装置。"}},{"en":"a particular position of the gears in a vehicle that gives a particular range of speed and power","cn":"挡","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"British English","sc":"in vehicle","ex":{"en":"first/second, etc. gear","cn":"一挡、二挡等"}},{"en":"the equipment or clothing needed for a particular activity","cn":"（某种活动的）设备，用具，衣服","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"equipment/clothes","ex":{"en":"climbing/fishing/sports gear","cn":"登山／钓鱼／运动装备"}},{"en":"clothes","cn":"衣服","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"informal","sc":"equipment/clothes","ex":{"en":"Her friends were all wearing the latest gear.","cn":"她的朋友都穿着最新款的衣服。"}},{"en":"the things that a person owns","cn":"所有物；财物","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"informal","sc":"possessions","ex":{"en":"I've left all my gear at Dave's house.","cn":"我把我所有的东西都留在戴夫家了。"}},{"en":"a machine used for a particular purpose","cn":"（特定用途的）器械，装置","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"machinery","ex":{"en":"lifting/towing/winding gear","cn":"起重／牵引／卷扬装置"}},{"en":"used to talk about the speed or effort involved in doing something","cn":"（做事的）速度，努力","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"British English","sc":"speed/effort","ex":{"en":"The party organization is moving into top gear as the election approaches.","cn":"随着选举的临近，这个政党的组织工作正在紧锣密鼓地进行。"}},{"en":"illegal drugs","cn":"毒品","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"slang","sc":"drugs"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"齿轮；传动装置；变速器","en":"The gears on a machine or vehicle are a device for changing the rate at which energy is changed into motion.","ex":{"en":"On hills, he must use low gears","cn":"在山上,他必须挂低速挡。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（某一特定活动的）设备，服装","en":"The gear involved in a particular activity is the equipment or special clothing that you use.","ex":{"en":"About 100 officers in riot gear were needed to break up the fight.","cn":"大约需要100名穿防暴服的警察前来制止这场斗殴。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"服装","en":"Gear means clothing.","ex":{"en":"I used to wear trendy gear but it just looked ridiculous.","cn":"我以前常穿新潮的衣服，但看上去却滑稽可笑。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"毒品；（尤指）海洛因","en":"Some people refer to illegal drugs, especially heroin, as gear .","ex":{"en":"Are these people using gear and amphetamines at the same time?","cn":"这些人同时服用海洛因和安非他明吗？"}},{"pos":"V-PASSIVE 被动动词","cn":"使为…而准备；使为了达到…而作好准备","en":"If someone or something is geared to or towards a particular purpose, they are organized or designed in order to achieve that purpose.","ex":{"en":"Colleges are not always geared to the needs of mature students","cn":"大学有时满足不了成人学生的需求。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：gear up"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Coming out of the final bend, the runner stepped up a gear to overtake the rest of the pack.","cn":"那名赛跑选手绕过最后一个弯道后开始加速，以图超越同组的其他选手。"},{"en":"( BrE ) The party organization is moving into top gear as the election approaches.","cn":"随着选举的临近，这个政党的组织工作正在紧锣密鼓地进行。"}]},"generously":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenərəsli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that shows that somebody is willing to give freely","cn":"慷慨地：以某种方式表明有人愿意自由地给予","ex":{"en":"Please give generously.","cn":"请慷慨解囊。"}},{"en":"using or providing more of something than is necessary","cn":"慷慨地：过度使用或提供不必要的","ex":{"en":"a dress that is generously cut (= uses plenty of material)","cn":"用料多的连衣裙"}},{"en":"kindly; in a way that shows that somebody is willing to see what is good about somebody/something","cn":"宽厚的；宽宏大量的；仁慈的","ex":{"en":"She speaks generously about everyone.","cn":"她对每个人都慷慨地谈论。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/generously__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/generously__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a dress that is generously cut (= uses plenty of material)","cn":"用料多的连衣裙"},{"en":"Please give generously.","cn":"请慷慨施与。"}]},"gene":{"oxford":{"phon":"dʒiːn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a unit inside a cell that controls a particular quality in a living thing that has been passed on from its parents","cn":"基因","ex":{"en":"a dominant/recessive gene","cn":"显性／隐性基因"}},{"en":"a first name for boys, short for Eugene","cn":"吉恩（男子名，Eugene缩写）","pos":""}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"基因","en":"A gene is the part of a cell in a living thing which controls its physical characteristics, growth, and development."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gene__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gene__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"I've always enjoyed music — it's in the genes.","cn":"我向来喜欢音乐，这是拜父母所赐。"},{"en":"genes that code for the colour of the eyes","cn":"为眼睛的颜色编码的基因"}]},"gentle":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gentle__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gentle__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒentl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"calm and kind; doing things in a quiet and careful way","cn":"文静的；慈祥的；温柔的；细心的","ex":{"en":"a kind and gentle man","cn":"和善文雅的男士"}},{"en":"not strong or extreme","cn":"温和的；徐缓的","ex":{"en":"a gentle breeze","cn":"和风"}},{"en":"having only a small effect; not strong or violent","cn":"平和的；柔和的","ex":{"en":"We went for a gentle stroll.","cn":"我们溜达去了。"}},{"en":"not steep or sharp","cn":"平缓的","ex":{"en":"a gentle slope/curve","cn":"平缓的斜坡／弯道"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"文静的；温和的；和蔼的","en":"Someone who is gentle is kind, mild, and calm.","ex":{"en":"My son was a quiet and gentle man who liked sports and enjoyed life","cn":"我儿子是个安静温和的人，喜欢运动和享受生活。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（动作）轻柔的，徐缓的","en":"Gentle actions or movements are performed in a calm and controlled manner, with little force.","ex":{"en":"...a gentle game of tennis","cn":"不激烈的网球比赛"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（天气）温和的； （尤指风）和煦的，微弱的","en":"If you describe the weather, especially the wind, as gentle, you mean it is pleasant and calm and not harsh or violent.","ex":{"en":"The blustery winds of spring had dropped to a gentle breeze.","cn":"呼啸的春风已经减弱，成了习习的微风。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（斜坡或弯道）平缓的，不陡的","en":"A gentle slope or curve is not steep or severe.","ex":{"en":"...gentle, rolling meadows","cn":"缓缓起伏的牧场"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"微热的","en":"A gentle heat is a fairly low heat.","ex":{"en":"Cook for 30 minutes over a gentle heat.","cn":"用文火煮30分钟。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He looks scary but he's really a gentle giant.","cn":"他看上去可怕，实际却是个性格温和的巨人。"},{"en":"He lived in a gentler age than ours.","cn":"他生活的时代比我们这个时代更平静祥和。"}]},"genius":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/genius__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/genius__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒiːniəs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"unusually great intelligence, skill or artistic ability","cn":"天才；天资；天赋","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the genius of Shakespeare","cn":"莎士比亚的天才"}},{"en":"a person who is unusually intelligent or artistic, or who has a very high level of skill, especially in one area","cn":"天才人物；（某领域的）天才","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a mathematical/comic, etc. genius","cn":"数学、喜剧等天才"}},{"en":"a special skill or ability","cn":"（特别的）才能，本领","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"He had a genius for making people feel at home.","cn":"他有一种能够使人感觉轻松自在的本领。"}},{"en":"showing unusually great intelligence, skill or artistic ability","cn":"天才；天资；天赋","ex":{"en":"a genius idea","cn":"天才的想法"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"天才；天赋；天资","en":"Genius is very great ability or skill in a particular subject or activity.","ex":{"en":"This is the mark of her real genius as a designer","cn":"这展现了她作为设计师的真正天赋。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"天才人物","en":"A genius is a highly talented, creative, or intelligent person.","ex":{"en":"Chaplin was not just a genius, he was among the most influential figures in film history.","cn":"卓别林不仅仅是天才，也是电影史上最有影响力的人物之一。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He had a genius for making people feel at home.","cn":"他有一种能够使人感觉轻松自在的本领。"},{"en":"He's a genius at organizing people.","cn":"他是人员组织方面的天才。"}]},"genus":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒiːnəs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a group into which animals, plants, etc. that have similar characteristics are divided, smaller than a family and larger than a species","cn":"（动植物等分类的）属"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尤指动植物的）属","en":"A genus is a class of similar things, especially a group of animals or plants that includes several closely related species."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/genus__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/genus__us_1.mp3"}},"geographically":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geographically__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geographically__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"geographically remote areas","cn":"地理上的边远地区"},{"en":"their geographical proximity to Japan (= nearness to Japan )","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒiːəˈɡræfɪkli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that is connected with how the physical features of a place are arranged","cn":"地形；地貌；地势","ex":{"en":"geographically remote areas","cn":"偏远地区"}},{"en":"in a way that is connected with how a particular aspect of life or society is influenced by geography or varies according to geography","cn":"地理环境","ex":{"en":"There is currently much interest in the ways in which public money is distributed geographically.","cn":"目前人们对公共资金的地理分配方式很感兴趣。"}}]}},"generation":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/generation__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/generation__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒenəˈreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"all the people who were born at about the same time","cn":"（统称）一代人，同代人，同辈人","g":"[countable + singular or plural verb]","ex":{"en":"the younger/older generation","cn":"年轻的一代；老一辈"}},{"en":"the average time in which children grow up, become adults and have children of their own, (usually considered to be about 30 years)","cn":"代，一代，一辈（通常认为大约 30 年）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Many more people go to university now than a generation ago.","cn":"现在上大学的人比上一代人多得多。"}},{"en":"a single stage in the history of a family","cn":"（家史中的）一代，一辈","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"stories passed down from generation to generation","cn":"世代相传的故事"}},{"en":"a group of people of similar age involved in a particular activity","cn":"一批，一届（从事特定活动的同龄人）","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"He influenced my generation more than any other actor.","cn":"他对我们这一代的影响比其他任何演员都大。"}},{"en":"a stage in the development of a product, usually a technical one","cn":"（产品发展，尤指技术方面的）代","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"fifth-generation computing","cn":"第五代计算机技术"}},{"en":"the production of something, especially electricity, heat, etc.","cn":"（尤指电、热等的）产生","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the generation of electricity","cn":"发电"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（尤指经历或观点相同的）一代人，同代人，同辈人","en":"A generation is all the people in a group or country who are of a similar age, especially when they are considered as having the same experiences or attitudes.","ex":{"en":"...the younger generation of Party members","cn":"年轻一代的党员"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"代，一代，一辈（通常认为大约是30年）","en":"A generation is the period of time, usually considered to be about thirty years, that it takes for children to grow up and become adults and have children of their own.","ex":{"en":"Within a generation flight has become the method used by many travellers.","cn":"就在不到一代人的时间里，坐飞机已经成了很多旅行者的出行方式。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（机械设备的设计和制造的）代","en":"You can use generation to refer to a stage of development in the design and manufacture of machines or equipment.","ex":{"en":"...a new generation of IBM/Apple computers.","cn":"新一代的IBM/苹果电脑"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（表示家庭成员拥有某国国籍的时间长短情况）第…代的","en":"Generation is used to indicate how long members of your family have had a particular nationality. For example, second generation means that you were born in the country you live in, but your parents were not.","ex":{"en":"...second generation Asians in Britain","cn":"英国的第二代亚洲移民"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"（能源的）产生","en":"Generation is also the production of a form of energy or power from fuel or another source of power such as water.","ex":{"en":"Japan has announced plans for a sharp rise in its nuclear power generation.","cn":"日本宣布了大幅增加核能发电的计划。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a first-/second-generation American (= a person whose family has lived in America for one/two generations)","cn":"第一/第二代美国人（家人在美国居住了一、二代者）"},{"en":"My generation have grown up without the experience of a world war.","cn":"我这一代人在成长过程中没有经历过世界大战。"}]},"geography":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geography__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geography__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dʒiˈɒɡrəfi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the scientific study of the earth’s surface, physical features, divisions, products, population, etc.","cn":"地理（学）","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"recent work in economic geography","cn":"经济地理学近期作品"}},{"en":"the way in which the physical features of a place are arranged","cn":"地形；地貌；地势","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"These streets had a very particular geography.","cn":"这些街道的地理位置非常特殊。"}},{"en":"the way in which a particular aspect of life or society is influenced by geography or varies according to geography","cn":"地理环境","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"The geography of poverty and the geography of voting are connected.","cn":"贫穷人口的地理分布与选票的地理分布是相联系的。"}},{"en":"a country, area or region","cn":"国家；地区","g":"[countable]","lab":"business","ex":{"en":"We are now operational across multiple geographies.","cn":"我们现在在多个地区开展业务。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"地理学","en":"Geography is the study of the countries of the world and of such things as the land, seas, climate, towns, and population."},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"地形；地貌","en":"The geography of a place is the way that features such as rivers, mountains, towns, or streets are arranged within it.","ex":{"en":"...policemen who knew the local geography.","cn":"熟悉当地地形的警察"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Kim knew the geography of the building and strode along the corridor.","cn":"金熟悉这栋建筑物的布局，大步流星地走在走廊上。"},{"en":"The geography of poverty and the geography of voting are connected.","cn":"贫穷人口的地理分布与选票的地理分布是相联系的。"}]},"geeky":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geeky__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geeky__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"愚蠢的；无能的；痴迷于电脑的","en":"If you describe someone as geeky, you think they look or behave like a geek.","ex":{"en":"...that geeky guy from the video-store counter.","cn":"在音像店上班的电脑迷"}}]},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈɡiːki","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"typical of a person who is boring, wears clothes that are not fashionable, does not know how to behave in social situations, etc.","cn":"闷蛋；土包子","ex":{"en":"a geeky guy/toy","cn":"一个极客/玩具"}},{"en":"very interested in a particular thing, especially computers or technology; showing this","cn":"怪癖","ex":{"en":"a bunch of geeky techies","cn":"一群极客技术人员"}}]}},"gesticulate":{"oxford":{"phon":"dʒeˈstɪkjuleɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to move your hands and arms about in order to attract attention or make somebody understand what you are saying","cn":"做手势；用手势表达；用动作示意","ex":{"en":"He gesticulated wildly at the clock.","cn":"他使劲指着钟打手势。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"做手势；用手势表达；用动作示意","en":"If you gesticulate, you make movements with your arms or hands, often while you are describing something that is difficult to express in words.","ex":{"en":"A man with a paper hat upon his head was gesticulating wildly","cn":"一个戴纸帽的男子在拼命地打手势。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gesticulate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gesticulate__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He gesticulated wildly at the clock.","cn":"他使劲指着钟打手势。"},{"en":"wild/frantic gesticulations","cn":"发狂似的手势"}]},"geese":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geese__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geese__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"(goose的复数)","en":"Geese is the plural of goose ."}]}},"german":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/german_1_gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/german_1_us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒɜːmən","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"from or connected with Germany","cn":"德国的"},{"en":"a person from Germany","cn":"德国人","g":"[countable]","pos":"noun"},{"en":"the language of Germany, Austria and parts of Switzerland","cn":"德语（德国、奥地利和瑞士部分地区的语言）","g":"[uncountable]","pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"德国的；德国人的；德语的","en":"German means belonging or relating to Germany.","ex":{"en":"...a cut in German interest rates.","cn":"德国利率的下调"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"德语","en":"German is the language used in Germany, Austria, and parts of Switzerland.","ex":{"en":"I heard a very angry man talking in German.","cn":"我听到一个怒不可遏的人说着德语。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"German history","cn":"德国历史"}]},"geared":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geared__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geared__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ɡɪəd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"designed or organized to achieve a particular purpose, or to be suitable for a particular group of people","cn":"旨在；适合于","ex":{"en":"The programme is geared to preparing students for the world of work.","cn":"本计划旨在为学生进入职场做准备。"}},{"en":"prepared and ready for something","cn":"（为…）做好准备，准备好","ex":{"en":"We have people on board geared up to help with any problems.","cn":"我们已得到人员支持，准备帮助解决任何问题。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"We have people on board geared up to help with any problems.","cn":"我们已让船上的人做好准备帮助解决任何问题。"},{"en":"The programme is geared to preparing students for the world of work.","cn":"本计划旨在为学生开始就业做准备。"}]},"germanic":{"oxford":{"phon":"dʒɜːˈmænɪk","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"connected with or considered typical of Germany or its people","cn":"德国的；德国人的；有德国（或德国人）特点的","ex":{"en":"She had an almost Germanic regard for order.","cn":"她简直像德国人一样讲究条理。"}},{"en":"connected with the language family that includes German, English, Dutch and Swedish among others","cn":"日耳曼语（族）的"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"德国人的；德国式的","en":"If you describe someone or something as Germanic, you think that their appearance or behaviour is typical of German people or things.","ex":{"en":"He asked in his Germanic English if I was enjoying France.","cn":"他操着一口带有德国腔的英语问我在法国玩得是否愉快。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"日耳曼文化的；日耳曼语的","en":"Germanic is used to describe the ancient culture and language of the peoples of northern Europe.","ex":{"en":"...the Germanic tribes of pre-Christian Europe.","cn":"基督教创立之前定居在欧洲的日耳曼部落"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/germanic__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/germanic__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She had an almost Germanic regard for order.","cn":"她简直像德国人一样讲究条理。"}]},"genetic":{"oxford":{"phon":"dʒəˈnetɪk","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"connected with genes (= the units in the cells of a living thing that control its physical characteristics) or genetics (= the study of genes)","cn":"基因的；遗传学的","ex":{"en":"genetic and environmental factors","cn":"遗传和环境因素"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"遗传的；基因的","en":"You use genetic to describe something that is concerned with genetics or with genes.","ex":{"en":"Cystic fibrosis is the most common fatal genetic disease in the United States.","cn":"囊性纤维化是美国最常见的致命遗传疾病。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/genetic__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/genetic__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"genetically engineered/determined/transmitted","cn":"转基因的；由基因决定的；遗传的"},{"en":"genetic and environmental factors","cn":"遗传和环境因素"}]},"gently":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gently__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gently__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒentli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that is soft and light, not strong, extreme or violent","cn":"温柔地；和缓地","ex":{"en":"She held the baby gently.","cn":"她轻轻地抱着婴儿。"}},{"en":"in a calm, kind and quiet way","cn":"温和地","ex":{"en":"‘You miss them, don't you?’ he asked gently.","cn":"“你想念他们，是吗？”他温和地问道。"}},{"en":"in a way that slopes very gradually","cn":"平缓地","ex":{"en":"The path ran gently down to the sea.","cn":"这条小路平缓地向大海延伸。"}},{"en":"used to tell somebody to be careful","cn":"（提醒对方小心）注意点，小心点，慢点","lab":"British English, informal，，","ex":{"en":"Gently! You'll hurt the poor thing!","cn":"小心点，你会弄痛这可怜的家伙！"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘You miss them, don't you?’ he asked gently. “","cn":"你想念他们，是吗？”他温和地问道。"},{"en":"Gently! You'll hurt the poor thing!","cn":"小心点，你会弄痛这可怜的家伙的！"}]},"gears":{"oxford":{"phon":"ɡɪə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"machinery in a vehicle that turns engine power (or power on a bicycle) into movement forwards or backwards","cn":"排挡；齿轮；传动装置"},{"en":"a particular position of the gears in a vehicle that gives a particular range of speed and power","cn":"挡"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gear__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gear__us_1.mp3"}},"genial":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/genial__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/genial__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒiːniəl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"friendly and cheerful","cn":"友好的；亲切的；欢快的","ex":{"en":"a genial person","cn":"和蔼可亲的人"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"友善的；真诚的；亲切的；和蔼可亲的","en":"Someone who is genial is kind and friendly.","ex":{"en":"Bob was always genial and welcoming","cn":"鲍勃总是那么友善热情。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"an atmosphere of warmth and geniality","cn":"热情友好的气氛"},{"en":"a genial person","cn":"和蔼可亲的人"}]},"geopolitical":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geopolitical__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geopolitical__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"地缘政治（学）的","en":"Geopolitical means relating to or concerned with geopolitics.","ex":{"en":"Hungary and Poland have suffered before because of their unfortunate geopolitical position on the European map.","cn":"匈牙利和波兰因其在欧洲地图上的极为不利的地缘政治位置而备受磨难。"}}]},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒiːəʊpəˈlɪtɪkl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"connected with the political relations between countries and groups of countries in the world, as influenced by their geography","cn":"地缘政治的，地缘政治学的","ex":{"en":"an uncertain economic and geopolitical situation","cn":"不确定的经济和地缘政治形势"}}]}},"gentleman":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gentleman__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gentleman__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒentlmən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a man who is polite and well educated, who has excellent manners and always behaves well","cn":"彬彬有礼的人；有教养的人；君子","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"You acted like a true gentleman.","cn":"你表现得像个真正的绅士。"}},{"en":"used to address or refer to a man, especially somebody you do not know","cn":"（称呼或指男子，尤其是不认识的）先生","g":"[countable, usually plural]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Ladies and gentlemen! Can I have your attention, please?","cn":"女士们，先生们，请大家注意！"}},{"en":"used to address or refer to a male member of a legislature, for example the House of Representatives","cn":"（对立法机构男议员的称呼）先生，阁下","lab":"North American English"},{"en":"a man from a high social class, especially one who does not need to work","cn":"有身份的人；绅士；富绅","lab":"old-fashioned","ex":{"en":"He retired to his estate and lived the life of a country gentleman.","cn":"他退隐庄园，过着乡绅的生活。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"有身份的人；绅士","en":"A gentleman is a man who comes from a family of high social standing.","ex":{"en":"...this wonderful portrait of English gentleman Joseph Greenway.","cn":"英国绅士约瑟夫·格林韦的精美画像"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"有教养的人；彬彬有礼的人；君子","en":"If you say that a man is a gentleman, you mean he is polite and educated, and can be trusted.","ex":{"en":"He was always such a gentleman.","cn":"他总是那么彬彬有礼。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT; N-VOC 可数名词；称呼名词","cn":"（对人礼貌的称呼）先生","en":"You can address men as gentlemen, or refer politely to them as gentlemen.","ex":{"en":"This way, please, ladies and gentlemen","cn":"女士们，先生们，这边请。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（口头的）君子协定，绅士协定","en":"A gentleman's agreement or a gentlemen's agreement is an informal agreement in which people trust one another to do what they have promised. The agreement is not written down and does not have any legal force.","ex":{"en":"We had no contract; it was done by a gentleman's agreement","cn":"我们没有签合同，就订了个君子协定。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a gentleman farmer (= one who owns a farm for pleasure, not as his main job)","cn":"乡绅（以拥有农场为乐趣，而不作为主业）"},{"en":"Ladies and gentlemen! Can I have your attention, please?","cn":"女士们，先生们，请大家注意！"}]},"get":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/get__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/get__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ɡet","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to receive something","cn":"收到；接到","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"receive/obtain","ex":{"en":"I got a call from Dave this morning.","cn":"今天早上我接到戴夫的电话。"}},{"en":"to obtain something","cn":"获得；得到","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"receive/obtain","ex":{"en":"He has just got a new job.","cn":"他刚找到一份新工作。"}},{"en":"to buy something","cn":"买；购买；采购","g":"[transitive]","lab":"North American English","sc":"receive/obtain","ex":{"en":"Where did you get that skirt?","cn":"你在哪儿买的那条裙子？"}},{"en":"to obtain or receive an amount of money by selling something","cn":"（卖某物）挣得，获得","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"receive/obtain","ex":{"en":"If you sell it at auction you can expect to get roughly £800.","cn":"如果你在拍卖会上出售它，预计可以得到大约 800 英镑。"}},{"en":"to go to a place and bring somebody/something back","cn":"去取；去带回","g":"[transitive]","sc":"bring","ex":{"en":"Quick—go and get a cloth!","cn":"快，去拿块布来！"}},{"en":"to achieve or be given a particular mark or grade in an exam","cn":"获得，得到（某考试成绩）","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"mark/grade","ex":{"en":"He got a ‘C’ in Chemistry and a ‘B’ in English.","cn":"他化学得了 C，英语得了 B。"}},{"en":"to start to develop an illness; to suffer from a pain, etc.","cn":"感染上；患上；遭受…之苦","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"illness","ex":{"en":"I got this cold off (= from) you!","cn":"我这感冒是被你传染的！"}},{"en":"to receive something as a punishment","cn":"受到；遭到；被判（刑）","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"punishment","ex":{"en":"He got ten years (= was sent to prison for ten years) for armed robbery.","cn":"他因持枪抢劫被判刑十年。"}},{"en":"to connect to the internet or a phone network; to receive broadcasts from a particular television or radio station","cn":"接收到；收听到；收看到","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"internet/phone/broadcasts","ex":{"en":"95 per cent of the UK can now get superfast broadband.","cn":"英国 95% 的地区现在可以接入超高速宽带。"}},{"en":"to be connected with somebody by phone","cn":"与（某人）电话联系；与（某人）通电话","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"contact","ex":{"en":"I wanted to speak to the manager but I got his secretary instead.","cn":"我想与经理说话，可接电话的却是他的秘书。"}},{"en":"to arrive at or reach a place or point","cn":"抵达，到达（某地或某点）","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"arrive","ex":{"en":"We got to San Diego at 7 o'clock.","cn":"我们 7 点钟到达了圣迭戈。"}},{"en":"to move to or from a particular place or in a particular direction, sometimes with difficulty; to make somebody/something do this","cn":"（使）到达，离开，沿…移动，艰难地移动","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"move/travel","ex":{"en":"The bridge was destroyed so we couldn't get across the river.","cn":"大桥已经毁坏，我们无法过河了。"}},{"en":"to use a bus, taxi, plane, etc.","cn":"搭乘，乘坐（公共汽车、出租车、飞机等）","g":"[transitive, no passive]","sc":"move/travel","ex":{"en":"We're going to be late—let's get a taxi.","cn":"我们要迟到了，咱们坐出租车吧。"}},{"en":"to reach a particular state or condition; to make somebody/something/yourself reach a particular state or condition","cn":"（使）达到，处于","sc":"state/condition","ex":{"en":"to get angry/bored/hungry/fat","cn":"发怒；生厌；感到饿；发胖"}},{"en":"to reach the point at which you feel, know, are, etc. something","cn":"开始（感觉到、认识到、成为）；达到…地步（或程度）","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"state/condition","ex":{"en":"After a time you get to realize that these things don't matter.","cn":"过段时间你会明白这些事情并不要紧。"}},{"en":"to cause something to happen or be done","cn":"使（某事）发生；使完成（某事）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"get something done","ex":{"en":"I must get my hair cut.","cn":"我得理发了。"}},{"en":"to make, persuade, etc. somebody/something to do something","cn":"使，让（某人或物做某事）；说服（某人做某事）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"make/persuade","ex":{"en":"I couldn't get the car to start this morning.","cn":"我今天早上没法让这汽车发动起来。"}},{"en":"to start doing something","cn":"开始；开始做","g":"[transitive]","sc":"start","ex":{"en":"I got talking to her.","cn":"我开始与她谈起来。"}},{"en":"to have the opportunity to do something","cn":"有机会（做某事）；得到（做某事的）机会","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"informal","sc":"opportunity","ex":{"en":"He got to try out all the new software.","cn":"他得以试用了所有的新软件。"}},{"en":"to prepare a meal","cn":"准备，做（饭）","g":"[transitive]","lab":"especially British English","sc":"meal","ex":{"en":"Who's getting the lunch?","cn":"谁来做午饭？"}},{"en":"to answer the phone or a door when somebody calls, knocks, etc.","cn":"接（电话）；应（门）","g":"[transitive, no passive]","lab":"informal","sc":"telephone/door","ex":{"en":"Will you get the phone?","cn":"你去接一下电话好吗？"}},{"en":"to catch or take hold of somebody, especially in order to harm or punish them","cn":"（尤指为伤害或惩罚）抓住，捉住，逮住","g":"[transitive]","lab":"informal","sc":"catch/hit","ex":{"en":"He was on the run for a week before the police got him.","cn":"他逃跑一周后警方才将他逮住。"}},{"en":"to hit or wound somebody","cn":"击中；使受伤","g":"[transitive]","sc":"catch/hit","ex":{"en":"The bullet got him in the neck.","cn":"子弹击中了他的颈部。"}},{"en":"to understand somebody/something","cn":"理解；明白","g":"[transitive, no passive]","lab":"informal","sc":"understand","ex":{"en":"I don't get you.","cn":"我搞不懂你的意思。"}},{"en":"used to say that something happens or exists","cn":"（表示发生或存在）","g":"[transitive, no passive]","lab":"informal","sc":"happen/exist","ex":{"en":"You get (= There are) all these kids hanging around in the street.","cn":"所有这些孩子都在街上闲逛。"}},{"en":"to make somebody feel confused because they do not understand something","cn":"使困惑；使迷惑；把…难住","g":"[transitive, no passive]","lab":"informal","sc":"confuse/annoy","ex":{"en":"‘What's the capital of Bhutan?’ ‘You've got me there!’ (= I don't know)","cn":"“不丹的首都在什么地方？”“你可把我难倒了！”"}},{"en":"to annoy somebody","cn":"使烦恼；使恼火","g":"[transitive, no passive]","lab":"informal","sc":"confuse/annoy","ex":{"en":"What gets me is having to do the same thing all day long.","cn":"使我感到烦恼的是整天都得干同样的事。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"V-LINK 连系动词","cn":"（与形容词连用）变得","en":"You use get with adjectives to mean 'become'. For example, if someone gets cold, they become cold, and if they get angry, they become angry.","ex":{"en":"The boys were getting bored","cn":"男孩子们开始感到厌烦。"}},{"pos":"V-LINK 连系动词","cn":"（用于表示状况或处境的表达中）陷入，处于","en":"Get is used with expressions referring to states or situations. For example, to get into trouble means to start being in trouble.","ex":{"en":"Half the pleasure of an evening out is getting ready","cn":"晚上外出时一半的乐趣在于出门前的准备。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使陷入，使处于（某种状况或处境）","en":"To get someone or something into a particular state or situation means to cause them to be in it.","ex":{"en":"I don't know if I can get it clean","cn":"我不知道自己是否能把它清理干净。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使…，让…（做）","en":"If you get someone to do something, you cause them to do it by asking, persuading, or telling them to do it.","ex":{"en":"...a long campaign to get US politicians to take the Aids epidemic more seriously","cn":"旨在使美国政界人士更加重视艾滋病流行的长期运动"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使做好；使完成","en":"If you get something done, you cause it to be done.","ex":{"en":"I might benefit from getting my teeth fixed","cn":"补牙可能对我有好处。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"来到，移动到（某处）","en":"To get somewhere means to move there.","ex":{"en":"I got off the bed and opened the door","cn":"我下床把门打开了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"到达；抵达","en":"When you get to a place, you arrive there.","ex":{"en":"Generally I get to work at 9.30am","cn":"我通常上午9点半到单位。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使移动到","en":"To get something or someone into a place or position means to cause them to move there.","ex":{"en":"Mack got his wallet out","cn":"麦克掏出钱包。"}},{"pos":"AUX 助动词","cn":"（常用作助动词，代替be构成被动语态）","en":"Get is often used in place of 'be' as an auxiliary verb to form passives.","ex":{"en":"Does she ever get asked for her autograph?","cn":"有人向她索要过签名吗？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（最终或逐渐）到达（某阶段）","en":"If you get to do something, you eventually or gradually reach a stage at which you do it.","ex":{"en":"Miller and Ferlinghetti got to be friends","cn":"米勒和费林盖蒂渐渐成了朋友。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"得以做；有机会做","en":"If you get to do something, you manage to do it or have the opportunity to do it.","ex":{"en":"How do these people get to be the bosses of major companies?","cn":"这些人是怎样成为大公司的老总的？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（让…）迅速行动起来/干起来/工作起来","en":"You can use get in expressions like get moving ,get going, and get working when you want to tell people to begin moving, going, or working quickly.","ex":{"en":"I aim to be off the lake before dawn, so let's get moving","cn":"我计划黎明前从湖畔出发，大家马上行动起来吧。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"到达（人生、事业的某一阶段）","en":"If you get to a particular stage in your life or in something you are doing, you reach that stage.","ex":{"en":"We haven't got to the stage of a full-scale military conflict","cn":"我们还未到全面军事冲突的地步。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"（用于谈论进展情况）（使…）取得进展/不会有进展","en":"You can use get to talk about the progress that you are making. For example, if you say that you are getting somewhere, you mean that you are making progress, and if you say that something won't get you anywhere, you mean it will not help you to progress at all.","ex":{"en":"Radical factions say the talks are getting nowhere and they want to withdraw","cn":"激进派宣称谈判没有进展，他们打算退出。"}},{"pos":"V-LINK 连系动词","cn":"到，接近（…时间）","en":"When it gets to a particular time, it is that time. If it is getting towards a particular time, it is approaching that time.","ex":{"en":"It got to after 1am and I was exhausted","cn":"已是凌晨一点多了，我累得筋疲力尽。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"对…产生影响；使痛苦","en":"If something that has continued for some time gets to you, it starts causing you to suffer.","ex":{"en":"That's the first time I lost my cool in 20 years in this job. This whole thing's getting to me.","cn":"干这份工作20年来，我头一次失去了冷静，这一切让我大伤脑筋。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使烦恼；使恼怒","en":"If something gets you, it annoys you.","ex":{"en":"What gets me is the attitude of so many of the people.","cn":"让我恼怒的是这么多人都是这样的态度。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"获得；得到","en":"If you get something that you want or need, you obtain it.","ex":{"en":"I got a job at the sawmill","cn":"我在锯木厂找了份工作。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"收到；得到","en":"If you get something, you receive it or are given it.","ex":{"en":"I'm getting a bike for my birthday","cn":"我过生日时会得到一辆自行车。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"去取；去带来","en":"If you get someone or something, you go and bring them to a particular place.","ex":{"en":"I came down this morning to get the newspaper","cn":"我今天上午过来取报纸。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"准备（饭菜）","en":"If you get a meal, you prepare it.","ex":{"en":"She was getting breakfast as usual.","cn":"她像往常一样在准备早餐。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"得出，计算出（结果）","en":"If you get a particular result, you obtain it from some action that you take, or from a calculation or experiment.","ex":{"en":"You could run that race again and get a different result each time","cn":"如果再参加一次那样的赛跑，每次的结果可能都不一样。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"卖得，售得（…钱）","en":"If you get a particular price for something that you sell, you obtain that amount of money by selling it.","ex":{"en":"He can't get a good price for his crops.","cn":"他的庄稼无法卖个好价钱。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"有（做…的时间或机会）","en":"If you get the time or opportunity to do something, you have the time or opportunity to do it.","ex":{"en":"You get time to think in prison","cn":"你在监狱里有时间反省。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"开始有（想法、印象或感受）","en":"If you get an idea, impression, or feeling, you begin to have that idea, impression, or feeling as you learn or understand more about something.","ex":{"en":"I get the feeling that you're an honest man","cn":"我开始觉得你是个诚实的人。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"得到，获得（感受或好处）","en":"If you get a feeling or benefit from an activity or experience, the activity or experience gives you that feeling or benefit.","ex":{"en":"Charles got a shock when he saw him","cn":"查尔斯见到他时大吃一惊。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（设法）看到","en":"If you get a look, view, or glimpse of something, you manage to see it.","ex":{"en":"Young men climbed on buses and fences to get a better view","cn":"为了看得更清楚些，年轻人爬上了公共汽车和围墙。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"有（…的天气）","en":"If a place gets a particular type of weather, it has that type of weather.","ex":{"en":"Riyadh got 25 mm of rain in just 12 hours","cn":"利雅得在12小时内降水就达25毫米。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"理解，明白（笑话或所说的话）","en":"If you get a joke or get the point of something that is said, you understand it.","ex":{"en":"Did you get that joke, Ann? I'll explain later","cn":"安，听懂那个笑话了吗？我过会儿会解释。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"染（病）；患（病）","en":"If you get an illness or disease, you become ill with it.","ex":{"en":"When I was five I got measles.","cn":"我5岁时出过麻疹。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"搭乘，乘（火车、公共汽车、飞机或船）","en":"When you get a train, bus, plane, or boat, you leave a place on a particular train, bus, plane, or boat.","ex":{"en":"It'll be two pounds to get the bus","cn":"乘公共汽车要花两英镑。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"捕获；猎杀","en":"If you get a person or animal, you succeed in catching, killing, or hitting them.","ex":{"en":"Take it easy. We've got him. He's not going to kill anyone else.","cn":"别担心，我们已经抓住他了，他不会再杀人。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"定期买（报刊、杂志等）","en":"If you get a newspaper or magazine, you regularly buy it.","ex":{"en":"We don't get a paper","cn":"我们不买报纸。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"接收；收到；收看到","en":"If you can get a particular radio or television channel, you are able to receive broadcasts from it on your radio or television.","ex":{"en":"I only get Channel 7.","cn":"我只能收看到第7频道。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"最…；（好…) 极了","en":"You can say that something is, for example, as good as you can get to mean that it is as good as it is possible for that thing to be.","ex":{"en":"Consort has a population of 714 and is about as rural and isolated as you can get.","cn":"康索特有714名居民，是极其偏僻的乡村地区。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"不能否认；无法否认","en":"If you say you can't get away from something or there is no getting away from something, you are emphasizing that it is true, even though people might prefer it not to be true.","ex":{"en":"There is no getting away from the fact that he is on the left of the party.","cn":"他属于该党左派的事实无法否认。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"休假；度假","en":"If you get away from it all, you have a holiday in a place that is very different from where you normally live and work.","ex":{"en":"...the ravishing island of Ischia, where rich Italians get away from it all.","cn":"意大利富人消遣度假的美丽岛屿伊斯基亚"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（表示蔑视、不同意或拒绝）滚开，去你的","en":"Get is used in rude expressions like get stuffed and get lost to express contempt, disagreement, or refusal to do something."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"你真是太走运了/你真是蠢得无可救药了","en":"You can say, for example, 'How lucky can you get?' or 'How stupid can you get? ' to show your surprise that anyone could be as lucky or stupid as the person that you are talking about.","ex":{"en":"I mean, how crazy can you get?","cn":"我是说，你真是太疯狂了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"叫…不要指望；叫…别做梦","en":"If you tell someone where to get off, you tell them in a rather rude way that you are not going to do or agree to what they want.","ex":{"en":"If somebody tried to do that to you, you'd just go right up to them and tell them where to get off.","cn":"如果有人想那样对待你，你就直截了当地告诉他们别做梦了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"有；存在","en":"You can use you get instead of 'there is' or 'there are' to say that something exists, happens, or can be experienced.","ex":{"en":"You get a lot of things like that now, don't you","cn":"你现在有很多那样的东西，是吧？"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：get about get across get ahead get along get around get around to get at get away get away with get back get back to get by get down get down to get in get in on get into get in with get off get off on get off with get on get on to get out get out of get over get over with get round get round to get through get together get up get up to"}]},"examples":[{"en":"You should get into the routine of saving the document you are working on every ten minutes.","cn":"你应该养成每十分钟将正在编辑的文件存盘一次的习惯。"},{"en":"Thousands of refugees will die if these supplies don't get through to them.","cn":"如果这些生活用品运不到，数以千计的难民就会死去。"}]},"gesture":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/gesture__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/gesture__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒestʃə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a movement that you make with your hands, your head or your face to show a particular meaning","cn":"手势；姿势；示意动作","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"He made a rude gesture at the driver of the other car.","cn":"他向另外那辆汽车的司机做了个粗野的手势。"}},{"en":"something that you do or say to show a particular feeling or intention","cn":"（表明感情或意图的）姿态，表示","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"They sent some flowers as a gesture of sympathy to the parents of the child.","cn":"他们送了一些花表示对孩子父母的同情。"}},{"en":"to move your hands, head, face, etc. as a way of expressing what you mean or want","cn":"做手势；用手势表示；用动作示意","ex":{"en":"‘I see you read a lot,’ he said, gesturing at the wall of books.","cn":"“看来你读的书很多。”他指着那一墙的书说道。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"手势；姿势；示意动作","en":"A gesture is a movement that you make with a part of your body, especially your hands, to express emotion or information.","ex":{"en":"Sarah made a menacing gesture with her fist","cn":"萨拉用拳头做了一个威胁性的动作。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（表明态度或意图的）姿态，表示","en":"A gesture is something that you say or do in order to express your attitude or intentions, often something that you know will not have much effect.","ex":{"en":"He questioned the government's commitment to peace and called on it to make a gesture of good will","cn":"他对政府致力和平的承诺提出质疑，并呼吁政府做出友好的表示。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"打手势；用手势表示；用动作示意","en":"If you gesture, you use movements of your hands or head in order to tell someone something or draw their attention to something.","ex":{"en":"I gestured towards the boathouse, and he looked inside","cn":"我朝船库方向示意，他便往里面瞧了瞧。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"We do not accept responsibility but we will refund the money as a gesture of goodwill.","cn":"我们不承担责任，不过我们愿意退款以表示我们的善意。"},{"en":"He made a rude gesture at the driver of the other car.","cn":"他向另外那辆汽车的司机做了个粗野的手势。"}]},"generalization":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/generalization__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/generalization__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒenrəlaɪˈzeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a general statement that is based on only a few facts or examples; the act of making such statements","cn":"概括；归纳；泛论","ex":{"en":"a speech full of broad/sweeping generalizations","cn":"通篇大而无当的发言"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"概括；概论；归纳","en":"A generalization is a statement that seems to be true in most situations or for most people, but that may not be completely true in all cases.","ex":{"en":"He is making sweeping generalisations to get his point across","cn":"为了让大家领会他的观点，他正在作全面的概括。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a speech full of broad/sweeping generalizations","cn":"满是概而论之话语的发言"},{"en":"Try to avoid generalization.","cn":"尽量避免泛泛而论。"}]},"geology":{"oxford":{"phon":"dʒiˈɒlədʒi","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the scientific study of the physical structure of the earth, including the origin and history of the rocks and soil of which the earth is made","cn":"地质学","g":"[uncountable]"},{"en":"the origin and history of the rocks and soil of a particular area","cn":"（某地区的）地质","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"the geology of the British Isles","cn":"不列颠群岛的地质"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"地质学","en":"Geology is the study of the Earth's structure, surface, and origins.","ex":{"en":"He was visiting professor of geology at the University of Jordan.","cn":"他是约旦大学的地质学客座教授。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"地质状况","en":"The geology of an area is the structure of its land, together with the types of rocks and minerals that exist within it.","ex":{"en":"...an expert on the geology of southeast Asia.","cn":"研究东南亚地质状况的专家"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/geology__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/geology__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"the geology of the British Isles","cn":"不列颠群岛的地质"},{"en":"a geological survey","cn":"地质勘察"}]},"general":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/general__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/general__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenrəl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"affecting all or most people, places or things","cn":"全体的；普遍的；总的","sc":"affecting all","ex":{"en":"books of general interest (= of interest to most people)","cn":"普遍感兴趣的书籍"}},{"en":"normal; usual","cn":"正常的；一般的；常规的","g":"[usually before noun]","sc":"usual","ex":{"en":"There is one exception to this general principle.","cn":"这个一般性原则有一例外。"}},{"en":"including the most important aspects of something; not exact or detailed","cn":"概括性的；大体的；笼统的","sc":"not exact","ex":{"en":"I check the bookings to get a general idea of what activities to plan.","cn":"我核查预订情况以便对计划安排些什么活动有个大体的想法。"}},{"en":"approximately, but not exactly, the direction/area mentioned","cn":"大致的，大概的（方向或地区）","sc":"not exact","ex":{"en":"They fired in the general direction of the enemy.","cn":"他们向敌军大致的方向开了枪。"}},{"en":"not limited to a particular subject, use or activity","cn":"非专门的；一般性的；普通的","sc":"not limited","ex":{"en":"a general hospital","cn":"综合医院"}},{"en":"not limited to one part or aspect of a person or thing","cn":"整体的；全身的；全面的","sc":"not limited","ex":{"en":"a general anaesthetic","cn":"全身麻醉"}},{"en":"highest in rank; chief","cn":"首席的；总管的","g":"[only before noun]","sc":"highest in rank","ex":{"en":"the general manager","cn":"总经理"}},{"en":"an officer of very high rank in the army or (in the US) the air force; the officer with the highest rank in the marines","cn":"将军；（陆军、海军陆战队或美国空军）上将","ex":{"en":"a four-star general","cn":"四星上将"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT; N-TITLE; N-VOC可数名词；头衔名词；称呼名词","cn":"将军；（通常指陆军）上将","en":"A general is a high-ranking officer in the armed forces, usually in the army.","ex":{"en":"The General's visit to Sarajevo is part of preparations for the deployment of extra troops.","cn":"将军造访萨拉热窝是在为增加兵力部署做准备。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"全体的；总的；普遍的","en":"If you talk about the general situation somewhere or talk about something in general terms, you are describing the situation as a whole rather than considering its details or exceptions.","ex":{"en":"The figures represent a general decline in employment.","cn":"这些数字显示就业人数总体在下降。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"一般性的；普通的","en":"You use general to describe several items or activities when there are too many of them or when they are not important enough to mention separately.","ex":{"en":"£2,500 for software is soon swallowed up in general costs","cn":"用于软件方面的2,500英镑很快就被一般性费用耗光了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"广泛的；普遍的","en":"You use general to describe something that involves or affects most people, or most people in a particular group.","ex":{"en":"The project should raise general awareness about bullying.","cn":"这个项目将会提高民众对恃强凌弱行径的认识。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"整体的；全面的","en":"If you describe something as general, you mean that it is not restricted to any one thing or area.","ex":{"en":"...a general ache radiating from the back of the neck.","cn":"从后颈部扩散到全身的疼痛"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（企业）综合的，业务广泛的","en":"A general business offers a variety of services or goods rather than just one particular kind.","ex":{"en":"They ran the general store and the farm dairy.","cn":"他们经营着杂货店和农场的乳品店。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（常用于头衔中）首席的，总管的，级别最高的","en":"General is used to describe a person's job, usually as part of their title, to indicate that they have complete responsibility for the administration of an organization or business.","ex":{"en":"He joined Sanders Roe, moving on later to become General Manager.","cn":"他加入了桑德斯·罗公司，后来一路晋升至总经理。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"（员工）普通的，非专业的，一般的","en":"General workers do a variety of jobs which require no special skill or training.","ex":{"en":"The farm employed a tractor driver and two general labourers.","cn":"农场雇用了一名拖拉机手和两名杂工。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（对某方面的知识或兴趣）一般的，泛泛的","en":"General is used to describe a person who has an average amount of knowledge or interest in a particular subject.","ex":{"en":"This book is intended for the general reader rather than the student.","cn":"这本书面向一般读者而非学生。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"总的来说；总体上来看；大体上","en":"You use in general to indicate that you are talking about something as a whole, rather than about part of it.","ex":{"en":"I think we need to improve our educational system in general","cn":"我认为有必要从整体上改进我们的教育体系。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"（指某一群体的大多数）总的来说，总体上","en":"You say in general to indicate that you are referring to most people or things in a particular group.","ex":{"en":"People in general will support us","cn":"总体而言，人们会支持我们的。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"通常；在多数情况下","en":"You say in general to indicate that a statement is true in most cases.","ex":{"en":"In general, it was the better-educated voters who voted Yes in the referendum.","cn":"通常是那些受教育程度较高的人在全民公决中投赞成票。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"This is a crucial year for your relationships in general and your love life in particular.","cn":"这一年总体上对你们的关系，特别是你们的爱情生活是非常关键的。"},{"en":"I check the bookings to get a general idea of what activities to plan.","cn":"我核查预订情况以便对计划安排些什么活动有个大体的想法。"}]},"generous":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/generous__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/generous__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenərəs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"giving or willing to give freely; given freely","cn":"慷慨的；大方的；慷慨给予的","ex":{"en":"The gallery was named after its most generous benefactor.","cn":"该画廊以其最慷慨的捐助者的名字命名。"}},{"en":"more than is necessary; large","cn":"丰富的；充足的；大的","ex":{"en":"a generous helping of meat","cn":"一大份肉"}},{"en":"kind in the way you treat people; willing to see what is good about somebody/something","cn":"宽厚的；宽宏大量的；仁慈的","ex":{"en":"a generous mind","cn":"宽阔的胸怀"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"（尤指在钱财上）慷慨的，大方的","en":"A generous person gives more of something, especially money, than is usual or expected.","ex":{"en":"German banks are more generous in their lending","cn":"德国银行的借贷条件更为宽松。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"宽厚的；仁慈的；宽宏大量的","en":"A generous person is friendly, helpful, and willing to see the good qualities in someone or something.","ex":{"en":"He was always generous in sharing his enormous knowledge","cn":"他从不吝啬与人分享自己渊博的知识。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"丰富的；大量的；充足的","en":"A generous amount of something is much larger than is usual or necessary.","ex":{"en":"...a generous six weeks of annual holiday","cn":"充裕的6个星期长的年假"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He wrote a very generous assessment of my work.","cn":"他给我写的工作评价多有赞誉之词。"},{"en":"It was generous of him to offer to pay for us both.","cn":"他主动为我们俩付钱，真是大方。"}]},"genuine":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/genuine__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/genuine__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenjuɪn","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"real; exactly what it appears to be; not artificial","cn":"真的；名副其实的","ex":{"en":"Is the painting a genuine Picasso?","cn":"这幅画是毕加索的真迹吗？"}},{"en":"sincere and honest; that can be trusted","cn":"真诚的；真心的；可信赖的","ex":{"en":"He made a genuine attempt to improve conditions.","cn":"他真心实意地努力改善环境。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"真正的；非伪造的；名副其实的","en":"Genuine is used to describe people and things that are exactly what they appear to be, and are not false or an imitation.","ex":{"en":"There was a risk of genuine refugees being returned to Vietnam.","cn":"存在将真正的难民遣返回越南的风险。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"真挚的；真诚的；诚挚的","en":"Genuine refers to things such as emotions that are real and not pretended.","ex":{"en":"There was genuine joy in this room","cn":"房间里洋溢着发自内心的快乐。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"真诚的；诚实可靠的；诚恳的","en":"If you describe a person as genuine, you approve of them because they are honest, truthful, and sincere in the way they live and in their relationships with other people.","ex":{"en":"She is very caring and very genuine.","cn":"她非常体贴，非常诚实可靠。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Fake designer watches are sold at a fraction of the price of the genuine article.","cn":"伪造的名牌手表以真品若干分之一的价格出售。"},{"en":"Only genuine refugees can apply for asylum.","cn":"只有真正的难民才能申请政治避难。"}]},"generated":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to produce or create sth","cn":"产生；引起"}]}},"gets":{"oxford":{"phon":"ɡet","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to receive sth","cn":"收到；接到"},{"en":"to obtain sth","cn":"获得；得到"}]}},"generating":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to produce or create sth","cn":"产生；引起"}]}},"genres":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈʒɒ̃rə","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a particular type or style of literature, art, film or music that you can recognize because of its special features （","cn":"文学、艺术、电影或音乐的）体裁，类型"}]}},"generations":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒenəˈreɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"all the people who were born at about the same time （","cn":"统称）一代人，同代人，同辈人"},{"en":"the average time in which children grow up, become adults and have children of their own, (usually considered to be about 30 years)","cn":"代，一代，一辈（通常认为大约 30 年）"}]}},"germans":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒɜːmən","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"from or connected with Germany","cn":"德国的"},{"en":"a person from Germany","cn":"德国人"}]}},"gentlemen":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒentlmən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a man who is polite and well educated, who has excellent manners and always behaves well","cn":"彬彬有礼的人；有教养的人；君子"},{"en":"( formal ) used to address or refer to a man, especially sb you do not know （","cn":"称呼或指男子，尤其是不认识的）先生"}]}},"generates":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenəreɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to produce or create sth","cn":"产生；引起"}]}},"generalize":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"概括；归纳；作出类推","en":"If you generalize, you say something that seems to be true in most situations or for most people, but that may not be completely true in all cases.","ex":{"en":"'In my day, children were a lot better behaved'. — 'It's not true, you're generalizing'","cn":"“我们那个时候，孩子们要比现在听话许多。”——“不一定，你只是在一概而论。”"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"推广；普及；扩大…的运用","en":"If you generalize something such as an idea, you apply it more widely than its original context, as if it was true in many other situations.","ex":{"en":"A child first labels the household pet cat as a 'cat' and then generalises this label to other animals that look like it.","cn":"孩子会先把家中的宠物猫称为“猫”，然后将其他像猫的动物都称为“猫”。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"an opinion or way of thinking about something that is simplistic treats difficult things in too simple a way","cn":""},{"en":"to say that something is true of all the people in a group simply because it is true of some of them","cn":""},{"en":"if someone sees things in black and white , they tend to judge people in a very simple way as being either completely bad or completely good, completely right or completely wrong etc","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 v 2 v 3 v","senses":[{"en":"To generalize is to use specific examples to make broader points. Generalizing makes large points, though they aren't always necessarily true."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERB + GENERALIZE can/could | be easy to, be possible to | be difficult to, be hard to, be impossible to | be dangerous to, be unsafe to, be","PREP. about It is impossible to generalize about such a complicated subject. | from We cannot generalize from these few examples."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/generalize0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/laadgeneralize.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It would be foolish to generalize from a single example.","cn":"仅从一个事例进行归纳的做法是愚蠢的。"},{"en":"It is dangerous to generalize about the poor.","cn":"对穷人一概而论是危险的。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenrəlaɪz","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to use a particular set of facts or ideas in order to form an opinion that is considered relevant to a different situation","cn":"概括；归纳","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"It would be foolish to generalize from a single example.","cn":"仅从一个事例进行归纳的做法是愚蠢的。"}},{"en":"to make a general statement about something and not look at the details","cn":"笼统地讲；概括地谈论","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"It is dangerous to generalize about the poor.","cn":"对穷人一概而论是危险的。"}},{"en":"to apply a theory, idea, etc. to a wider group or situation than the original one","cn":"扩大…的运用；将…类推到（较大的范围）","g":"[transitive, often passive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"These conclusions cannot be generalized to the whole country.","cn":"这些结论不能推及全国。"}}]}},"gender":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"性；性别","en":"A person's gender is the fact that they are male or female.","ex":{"en":"Women are sometimes denied opportunities solely because of their gender.","cn":"妇女有时仅仅因为性别而无法获得种种机会。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（统称）男性，女性","en":"You can refer to all male people or all female people as a particular gender.","ex":{"en":"While her observations may be true about some men, they could hardly apply to the entire gender.","cn":"虽然她的评论就某些男人而言可能是正确的，但绝不适用于所有男性。"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（语法中名词、代词或形容词的）性","en":"In grammar, the gender of a noun, pronoun, or adjective is whether it is masculine, feminine, or neuter. A word's gender can affect its form and behaviour. In English, only personal pronouns such as 'she', reflexive pronouns such as 'itself', and possessive determiners such as 'his' have gender.","ex":{"en":"In both Welsh and Irish the word for 'moon' is of feminine gender.","cn":"在威尔士语和爱尔兰语中，表示“月亮”的词是阴性的。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone's sex is whether they are male or female","cn":""},{"en":"someone's gender is whether they are male or female - used especially in writing about politics and society, or in job advertisements","cn":""},{"en":"relating to the differences between male and female or the characteristics of men or women","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"The noun gender refers to the state of being male or female. Danica Patrick is someone who has broken many gender barriers by being a successful female race-car driver in a male-dominated sport."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["GENDER + NOUN relations | differences, divisions She examines the interplay between changing gender divisions and urban change. | bias, imba"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/f/gender0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/gender.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"If in doubt, ask your doctor. He/she can give you more information.","cn":"如有疑问请向你的医生咨询，他/她会给你更多的信息。"},{"en":"In French the adjective must agree with the noun in number and gender.","cn":"法语中形容词必须在数和性上与名词一致。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒendə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of being male or female, especially when considered with reference to social and cultural differences, rather than differences in biology; members of a particular gender as a group","cn":"性别（尤指社会和文化差异，而非生理差异）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"issues of class, race and gender","cn":"阶级、种族和性别问题"}},{"en":"each of the classes (masculine, feminine and sometimes neuter) into which nouns, pronouns and adjectives are divided; the division of nouns, pronouns and adjectives into these different genders. Different genders may have different endings, etc.","cn":"性（阳性、阴性和中性，不同的性有不同的词尾等）","g":"[countable, uncountable]","lab":"grammar","ex":{"en":"In French the adjective must agree with the noun in number and gender.","cn":"法语中形容词必须在数和性上与名词一致。"}}]}},"generosity":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"慷慨；大方","en":"If you refer to someone's generosity, you mean that they are generous, especially in doing or giving more than is usual or expected.","ex":{"en":"There are stories about his generosity, the massive amounts of money he gave to charities.","cn":"有传闻说他向慈善机构慷慨解囊，捐献巨款。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who is generous gives money or presents to other people, and you think it is kind and good of them to do this","cn":""},{"en":"generous behaviour","cn":""},{"en":"a generous attitude, or generous behaviour","cn":"慷慨﹐大方"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Generosity is a quality that's a lot like unselfishness — someone showing generosity is happy to give to or share time, money, food, or whatever with others."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. extraordinary, great, unusual","VERB + GENEROSITY show (sb) He thanked them for the extraordinary generosity they had shown. | take advantage of Their guests took advantage","PREP. ~ to/towards their great generosity to the school","PHRASES an act of generosity, generosity of spirit She showed an unusual generosity of spirit to those who had opposed her. | thanks to the "]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/generosity0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/generosity.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He treated them with generosity and thoughtfulness.","cn":"他待他们宽容大度、体贴周到。"},{"en":"I shall never forget the generosity shown by the people of Bataisk.","cn":"我永远也不会忘记巴泰斯克人的慷慨大方。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌdʒenəˈrɒsəti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of being generous (= willing to do kind things or give somebody money, gifts or time freely)","cn":"慷慨；大方；宽宏大量","ex":{"en":"He treated them with generosity and thoughtfulness.","cn":"他待他们宽容大度、体贴周到。"}}]}},"genocide":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"种族灭绝；大屠杀","en":"Genocide is the deliberate murder of a whole community or race.","ex":{"en":"They have alleged that acts of genocide and torture were carried out.","cn":"他们声称实施了大屠杀和酷刑。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"when a large number of people are easily killed, because they are not able to defend themselves","cn":""},{"en":"when a large number of people are killed in a very cruel or violent way","cn":""},{"en":"when a large number of people are violently killed, especially in a war - used especially in newspapers","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Genocide refers to the systematic destruction of a race or cultural group. In the Rwandan genocide of 1994, members of one ethnic group, the Hutus, killed some 850,000 Tutsis in an attempt to wipe them out completely."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. mass Refugees gave accounts of the mass genocide. | cultural","PREP. ~ against genocide against ethnic minorities • Note at CRIME (for verbs)"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/genocide0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/0/genocide.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The military leaders were accused of genocide.","cn":"军方领导人被指控实施种族大屠杀。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenəsaɪd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the murder of a large number of people from a particular nation or ethnic group, with the aim of destroying that nation or group","cn":"种族灭绝；大屠杀","ex":{"en":"Refugees gave accounts of the mass genocide.","cn":"难民们描述了大规模种族屠杀的场面。"}}]}},"geneva":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"a city in Switzerland which is the main base for the red cross , the world health organization , and several other important international organizations. It is on the shore of Lake Geneva, one of the largest lakes in Europe.","cn":""}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/lpd_geneva.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/p028-000005328.mp3"}},"gem":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"宝石","en":"A gem is a jewel or stone that is used in jewellery.","ex":{"en":"...a gold mask inset with emeralds and other gems.","cn":"一张镶有翡翠和其他宝石的金面具"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"难能可贵的人（或物）；令人非常惬意的人（或事物）；精品","en":"If you describe something or someone as a gem, you mean that they are especially pleasing, good, or helpful.","ex":{"en":"...a gem of a hotel, Castel Clara","cn":"卡斯特尔·克拉拉酒店，酒店中的明珠"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a valuable stone, such as a diamond","cn":""},{"en":"a rare and valuable jewel such as a diamond or an emerald","cn":""},{"en":"a jewel that has been cut into a special shape","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. precious, priceless","PHRASES dripping with gems a millionairess dripping with gems and pearls | encrusted/studded with gems a belt studded with priceless gems 2 ","ADJ. little | absolute, real The second side of their new album contains some real gems. | hidden She worked in the antiques trade, searchin","PHRASES a gem of a sth This is a little gem of a flower."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/gem0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/gem.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"This picture is the gem (= the best) of the collection.","cn":"这幅画是收藏中的极品。"},{"en":"She's a real gem!","cn":"她真是难能可贵！"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dʒem","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a precious stone that has been cut and polished and is used in jewellery","cn":"（经切割打磨的）宝石","lab":"less frequent","ex":{"en":"a crown studded with gems","cn":"镶有宝石的皇冠"}},{"en":"a person, place or thing that is especially good","cn":"难能可贵的人；风景优美的地方；美妙绝伦的事物","ex":{"en":"This picture is the gem (= the best) of the collection.","cn":"这幅画是收藏中的极品。"}}]}},"germ":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"细菌；病菌","en":"A germ is a very small organism that causes disease.","ex":{"en":"Chlorine is widely used to kill germs.","cn":"氯气被广泛用于杀菌。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"起源；发端；萌芽","en":"The germ of something such as an idea is something which developed or might develop into that thing.","ex":{"en":"The germ of an idea took root in Rosemary's mind","cn":"罗斯玛丽心里萌生了一个念头。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a very small living thing that can make you ill","cn":"病菌﹐细菌"},{"en":"the early stage of an idea, feeling etc that may develop into something bigger and more important","cn":"观念/理论/感情等的萌芽"},{"en":"the part of a plant or animal that can develop into a new plant or animal","cn":"胚原基﹐胚芽"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A germ is a tiny life form that spreads disease. Germs are also small things that grow into larger things — whether animals, plants, or ideas."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. virulent The epidemic was caused by a particularly virulent flu germ. | flu, typhoid, etc.","VERB + GERM carry Children carry all kinds of germs home from school. | harbour Cracks and scratches in work surfaces can harbour germs. | d","GERM + NOUN warfare"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/a/brelasdegerm.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/germ.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Here was the germ of a brilliant idea.","cn":"一个绝妙的主意就是从这里萌发的。"},{"en":"Dirty hands can be a breeding ground for germs.","cn":"脏手可能滋生病菌。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"dʒɜːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a very small living thing that can cause infection and disease","cn":"微生物；细菌；病菌","g":"[countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"Disinfectant kills germs.","cn":"消毒剂可杀菌。"}},{"en":"an early stage of the development of something","cn":"起源；发端；萌芽","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"Here was the germ of a brilliant idea.","cn":"一个绝妙的主意就是从这里萌发的。"}},{"en":"the part of a plant or an animal that can develop into a new one","cn":"胚芽；胚原基；芽孢；胚胎","g":"[countable]","lab":"biology","ex":{"en":"The germ is the embryo of the new plant.","cn":"胚芽是新植物的胚胎。"}}]}},"george":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"used when you are pleasantly surprised","cn":""}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/george_n.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/laadgeorge.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"By George, I think you're right!","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"dʒɔːdʒ","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"a first name for boys","cn":"乔治（男子名）"}]}},"generator":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"发电机","en":"A generator is a machine which produces electricity."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"促使…发生的人（或事物）；产生者","en":"A generator of something is a person, organization, product, or situation which produces it or causes it to happen.","ex":{"en":"The US economy is still an impressive generator of new jobs","cn":"美国经济依然在创造着数量惊人的新就业机会。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a machine that produces electricity","cn":"发电机"},{"en":"a company that produces electricity","cn":"电力公司"},{"en":"something that produces something else","cn":"产生者"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. diesel, gas, petrol, steam, wind | electrical, electricity, power","VERB + GENERATOR drive, power A water turbine drives the generator.","GENERATOR + VERB deliver sth The wind generator delivers 120 watts in a strong breeze."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/generator0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/generator.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The museum uses smells and smoke generators to create atmosphere.","cn":"博物馆利用气味和烟雾生成器制造气氛。"},{"en":"The factory's emergency generators were used during the power cut.","cn":"工厂应急发电机在停电期间用上了。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈdʒenəreɪtə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a machine for producing electricity","cn":"发电机","ex":{"en":"The factory's emergency generators were used during the power cut.","cn":"工厂应急发电机在停电期间用上了。"}},{"en":"a machine for producing a particular substance","cn":"发生器","ex":{"en":"The museum uses smells and smoke generators to create atmosphere.","cn":"博物馆利用气味和烟雾发生器制造气氛。"}},{"en":"a person or thing that creates something","cn":"生成者；创造者","ex":{"en":"The company is a major generator of jobs.","cn":"这家公司创造了相当多的就业机会。"}},{"en":"a company that produces electricity to sell to the public","cn":"电力公司","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"the UK’s major electricity generator","cn":"英国的主要电力公司"}}]}},"genetics":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"遗传学","en":"Genetics is the study of heredity and how qualities and characteristics are passed on from one generation to another by means of genes."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the study of how the qualities of living things are passed on in their gene s","cn":"遗传学"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Genetics is the study of the traits people and other animals inherit from their family through DNA."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. evolutionary | molecular | medical | human, plant | population | Mendelian","PHRASES the science of genetics • Note at SUBJECT (for verbs and nouns)"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/brelasdegenetics.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/genetics.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"dʒəˈnetɪks","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the scientific study of the ways in which different characteristics are passed from each generation of living things to the next","cn":"遗传学"}]}}});
